{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"talented-portable-sow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThe MCP gate singleflight key (`src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py` `compute_key`) hashes gate,\ncanonical ticket id, code basis SHA, variant, and readonly flag. Both completion call sites in\n`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` pass `variant=f\"graph={graph};source={source or 'attested'}\"`:\n`verify_completion_start` (~line 313) and the sync `verify_completion` tool (~line 420). The\nticket's text is not in the key. So while a completion check of ticket T is in flight, editing T\nand starting another check returns the SAME run, which read the old text when it started.\n\nThis is the same mechanism fixed for plan review in next-embattled-geese (3b27-8f4b, Gerrit\n3040), which added the material fingerprint via `_plan_review_variant`.\n\nHarm is worse than for plan review. Plan review re-checks its material under the store lock\nbefore signing; completion does not (bug daredevil-marginal-dodo, 0521-7e68). The attached\npre-edit run signs a PASS whose manifest binds the POST-edit material, and a close then reuses\nit. Dedup therefore routes the author's correct \"edit, then re-verify\" into that hole: they\nreceive a signed PASS for text that was never verified. This ticket stops the re-verify from\nattaching; daredevil-marginal-dodo fixes what the attached run signs. Both are needed; this one\ndoes not depend on the other.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Add `_completion_variant(ticket_id, graph, source)` in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` returning\n   `f\"graph={graph};source={source or 'attested'};material={fp}\"`, with `fp` from\n   `rebar.llm.plan_review.attest.current_material_fingerprint(ticket_id)` (light read, no LLM).\n2. Use it at both completion call sites. In `verify_completion_start` compute it inside the\n   worker thread (same as `review_plan_start`), not on the event loop.\n3. `material=None` arm: `current_material_fingerprint_impl` returns None on a read failure\n   outside a pinned view, so this arm is live. Such calls dedup only with each other, never\n   with a run keyed on a real fingerprint.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py`: a blocked `verify_completion_start` run is in\n  flight, the description is edited, a second start returns a NEW job whose gate call sees the\n  edited text. Fails on origin/main 82a91a89f1d.\n- [ ] Same through the sync `verify_completion` tool: after an edit, a concurrent call runs the\n  gate a second time. Fails on origin/main.\n- [ ] Unchanged material still dedups: the existing\n  `test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once[verify_completion]` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] Key-shape test: different fingerprints give different variants; a None fingerprint gives\n  `graph=None;source=attested;material=None`, distinct from both.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py -p no:randomly -q\nmake lint && make typecheck && make verify\n```","id":"c912-f274-cef7-4089","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["mcp","completion-gate","gate-integrity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"verify_completion dedup key omits ticket material, so a check started after a description edit attaches to the pre-edit run"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792379213599330001,"uuid":"6a85da40-cfee-4f60-b2db-c4a665aefd60"}